4. Supported Files

    The upload workflow was designed to support common prescription formats such as:

    JPG
    PNG
    PDF

    The interface provides users with clear information about accepted formats before uploading.

5. File Selection Workflow

    The implemented workflow follows:

    User opens Prescription Upload
              ↓
    Select / Upload Prescription
              ↓
    File Validation
              ↓
    File Preview / File Information
              ↓
    User Confirms Submission
              ↓
    Prescription Submitted
              ↓
    Pharmacy Review
              ↓
    Prescription Processing

6. File Validation

    Validation was included to prevent invalid files from being submitted.

    Validation can check:

    File format.
    File size.
    File availability.
    Required upload field.
    Valid prescription attachment.

    If validation fails, the user receives a clear message.

    Example:

    Invalid file format.

    Please upload a JPG, PNG, or PDF prescription.

7. Prescription Preview

    After selecting a prescription, the interface displays the selected document/file information before final submission.

    For supported image files, a preview can be displayed.

    Example:

    Prescription_2026.jpg

    [ Preview ]

    [ Remove ]    [ Submit Prescription ]

    This gives users an opportunity to verify that they selected the correct document.

8. Upload Status

    Added user feedback for different upload states.

    Uploading
    Uploading prescription...
    Successful
    ✓ Prescription uploaded successfully.
    Failed
    Unable to upload prescription.
    Please try again.

    This improves transparency throughout the upload process.

9. Prescription Submission

    After successful validation, the user can submit the prescription.

    The submission process stores the prescription information and makes it available for pharmacy-side review.

    The workflow is designed to prevent incomplete submissions and provide confirmation after successful upload.

10. Pharmacy Review Workflow

     The uploaded prescription can follow a review process:

     Submitted
         ↓
     Under Review
         ↓
     Verified
         ↓
     Processing
         ↓
     Completed

     If the prescription cannot be processed, an appropriate status can be applied for further customer action.

